From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PandaSpigot <pandaspigot@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:20:55 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Add a spatial player index for recipient lookups

Chunk now maintains a set of players in that chunk. World nearby-player lookups, PlayerList.sendPacketNearby, and EntityTracker use chunk-indexed lookups instead of scanning all players/entities.

EntityTrackerEntry.track() now receives only nearby players, scans them on movement, and removes out-of-range viewers from its (small) trackedPlayers set instead of scanning all players. Initial entity tracking and per-player updates also use nearby chunks.

For 1,000 players and 10,000 entities:
- nearby lookup range 64: 1,000 -> ~82 candidate checks (92% fewer)
- nearby lookup range 128: 1,000 -> ~293 candidate checks (71% fewer)
- per moved player entity sweep: 10,000 -> ~332 checks (97% fewer)
- per moving entity track() scan: 1,000 -> ~82 checks (92% fewer)

